5. Benefits and Challenges

A. Benefits of Automation

1. Faster Software Delivery

Automated building, testing and deployment reduce the time required to release new features and bug fixes.

2. Improved Software Quality

Automated testing helps identify errors early and improves application reliability.

3. Reduced Human Errors

Automation reduces mistakes during manual testing and deployment processes.

B. Challenges

1. Initial Setup Complexity

Setting up CI/CD pipelines, automation tools and deployment environments requires technical knowledge and initial effort.

2. Tool Integration

Integrating different development, testing and deployment tools can be challenging and may require additional configuration.

3. Continuous Maintenance

CI/CD pipelines need regular monitoring and maintenance to ensure that automated processes work correctly.

6. Conclusion

DevOps practices and CI/CD pipelines provide an effective solution for automating the development and deployment of the online shopping application.

By automating code integration, building, testing and deployment, the company can release updates faster and reduce human errors.

It also improves software quality, team collaboration and application reliability.

Therefore, implementing DevOps and CI/CD practices helps the company develop and maintain its online shopping application more efficiently.

